  "system": {
    "description": {
      "gm": "",
      "value": "<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-bidi-font-weight:bold\">The Hezonkhai blood runs strong through you, forged from endless conflict fueled by the divine right of war. You have a substantially bulkier and muscular body, and are of greater height and strength than the Eronkhai. You have a pronounced underbite and tusks. Your fist unarmed attacks deal 1d6 damage and you do not suffer penalties for attacking lethally with them. You also gain a tusks unarmed attack that deals 1d6 piercing damage; they are in the brawling group and have finesse and unarmed traits.</span></p>"
